#!/usr/bin/env too

## Generate CHANGELOG.md following Keep a Changelog 1.1.0.
agic update_changelog(since?: Text, version?: Text, date?: Text):
  Read AGENTS.md. Maintain CHANGELOG.md as the canonical user-facing change
  record using Keep a Changelog 1.1.0. Reuse the current dedicated worktree and
  write only CHANGELOG.md, in English; do not invoke this runnable recursively,
  commit, push, create issues or pull requests, tag, or publish. Reuse the record
  for GitHub Release notes; do not create separate release notes or
  known-limitations documents.

  Inputs: baseline {{since}}, release version {{version}}, release date {{date}}.
  With neither version nor date, update Unreleased. Require both for release
  preparation; validate the version against the project and date as YYYY-MM-DD
  before writing. If the release heading, date, and comparison links already
  match and Unreleased is empty, return the no-change response without auditing
  history. Use default mode to refresh coverage.

  Verify the supplied baseline or use the latest release tag reachable from
  HEAD. Inspect only relevant repository files, commits through HEAD, tags,
  and pending diffs. If CHANGELOG.md is absent, create it from this evidence,
  state the tracking baseline, and do not restore or backfill historical records.

  Preserve existing entries and links; prepend only missing information.
  Correct records only for verified factual errors or necessary migration
  guidance, and report each correction. Leave complete records unchanged.
  For release preparation, move verified Unreleased entries unchanged into the
  target version and date, keeping Unreleased above it. The target tag may be
  unpublished. Compare the baseline to the target tag and the target to HEAD
  for Unreleased. If the target section exists, add only missing changes that
  belong to it; preserve later releases.

  Describe one user-visible outcome per new entry in one sentence of at most
  30 words. For breaking changes, allow up to two sentences and 50 words total,
  including a concrete migration step. Group related implementation changes by
  their impact on users. Include technical names only when needed for users to
  act; link verified pull requests or documentation for details instead of
  listing types, fields, methods, options, or schema internals. Omit internal-only
  work.

  Check every new entry against these sentence and word limits before saving.
  Verify claims and links, then run git diff --check on the final edits.
  Stop when verified.
  If no update is needed, reply only:
  "CHANGELOG.md is up to date. No changes made."
  Otherwise, report additions and necessary corrections in at most three short
  bullets and 60 words total; include a blocker only if it prevents completion.
